# The working tree is CRLF throughout (core.autocrlf=true) and that is left
# alone. This file exists for one directory.
#
# scripts/prerender.mjs writes each fragment as a single LF-terminated line, so
# after `npm run prerender` git reported all seven as modified even when the
# output was byte-identical to what was committed — `git diff --exit-code` said
# clean while `git status` said ` M`. That is a false signal on exactly the
# files where a true one matters: the fragments go stale SILENTLY when shared UI
# changes and nobody re-runs the capture, and a directory that always looks
# dirty is a directory whose dirtiness nobody reads.
#
# Pinning them to LF makes the checked-out form match what the script writes, so
# a modified fragment now means the render actually changed.
prerendered/*.html text eol=lf
